{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1343408-how-to-deal-with-pack-npc","id":1343408,"title":"How to deal with pack npc","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-24T07:11:22-07:00","id":1343408,"title":"How to deal with pack npc","content":"How do you guys deal with the packs npc? My group of 2 players each have 1 wolf blooded and animal companions and their spirit reflection and their spirit totem. Their is also a couple of human unaware of their supernatural lineage. <br /> <br /> I am not really a fan of being the Storyteller with his own character. So i am thinking of giving my players the sheets of their pack mates. But in a ambush situation or a combat situation how do you roll for the npc? I don't really want to roll 6 time for wits + composure for each pack mate... ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T09:56:19-07:00","id":1343449,"title":"","content":"You could make a decision about their initiative being behind their relative werewolf. Or roll for all of them with one die.<br /> <br /> The Pack book gets more into it, what everyone does during the hunt, after the hunt, and during downtime, but aside from acting as support characters and touchstones, you can also use them for troupe play. So if the shaman is busy preparing for a ritual, his wolf-blooded can go with the pack to do some socializing and things that he's good at and perhaps the shaman isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T10:12:33-07:00","id":1343453,"title":"","content":"The role playing part is not necessarily the problem more the mechanics behind a bunch of npc, i just don't Want to cut the flow by rolling for to much npc individually. <br /> <br /> Should i round their stats up and do just one attack roll? One wits + composure roll etc? <br /> <br /> How do you deal with combat if you have a group of 4 players and each has a wolf blooded and a totem and maybe extra humans or spirits? A pack can grow pretty large does the books have some mechanics for dealing with pack npcs that i missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T11:24:43-07:00","id":1343470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightsyko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1343408-how-to-deal-with-pack-npc?p=1343453#post1343453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The role playing part is not necessarily the problem more the mechanics behind a bunch of npc, i just don't Want to cut the flow by rolling for to much npc individually. <br /> <br /> Should i round their stats up and do just one attack roll? One wits + composure roll etc? <br /> <br /> How do you deal with combat if you have a group of 4 players and each has a wolf blooded and a totem and maybe extra humans or spirits? A pack can grow pretty large does the books have some mechanics for dealing with pack npcs that i missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered using the Down and Dirty Combat mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T12:01:30-07:00","id":1343476,"title":"","content":"How often do you expect this problem to come up? Generally a pack only has werewolves (i.e. the PCs) in the hunting party, leaving behind the rest of the pack when they're expecting combat. And most enemies would prefer not to engage the entire pack at the same time. If you feel it's going to be too much of a hassle with having combat scenes with the entire pack, you could just avoid having such scenes. Just explain to your players that bringing non-uratha on hunts is generally avoided because it puts them at extreme risk, considering their lack of regeneration and the fact that werewolves in Basu-Im can and will go after their own pack mates unless they're also in Basu-Im, should there be no fitting enemies to go for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T15:20:35-07:00","id":1343504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1343408-how-to-deal-with-pack-npc?p=1343470#post1343470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered using the Down and Dirty Combat mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but down and dirty is still a contested rolls so i would have to roll for each pack npcs vs an attack from the enemy so if i have 2 wolf blodded i need to make 4 rolls if they have their own enemy to fight<br /> <br /> I find it odd that in a game where the pack is the main subject of the game and where in character creation it is in the rules to create npcs for the players their is no game mechanics to use them. Maybe i missed the spot, if so plz tell me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think i will homebrew a pack dice pool a bit how renown for spirtis works and roll that?<br /> <br /> Thabk you for all the help, i know exalted has some good group fighting rules might check that out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T17:39:23-07:00","id":1343521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightsyko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1343408-how-to-deal-with-pack-npc?p=1343504#post1343504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but down and dirty is still a contested rolls so i would have to roll for each pack npcs vs an attack from the enemy so if i have 2 wolf blodded i need to make 4 rolls if they have their own enemy to fight</div> </div> </div> </div>Down and Dirty resolves <i>the entire combat</i> in one contested roll. Use the best concerned combatants with a compatible intent for killing or repelling the attackers or for defending or aiding the escape of the less durable pack members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find it odd that in a game where the pack is the main subject of the game and where in character creation it is in the rules to create npcs for the players their is no game mechanics to use them. Maybe i missed the spot, if so plz tell me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>\u2026There's an entire section providing game mechanics for using your secondary characters. What you're asking about is a separate matter from how to use individual pack members; in a game of Werewolf, as Tessie points out, werewolves generally deal with physical threats on their own.<br /> <br /> You might borrow bits of the krewe mechanics from Geist, if you just want to model a bunch of people fighting as a single abstracted action, but in general the solution to dealing with mortal allies on the field is to get them off the field as quickly as possible before another werewolf gets them, you get them by mistake, or an inhuman thing with an unhealthy interest in their bodily contents gets too close for comfort too soon for you to do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T09:12:45-08:00","id":1357370,"title":"","content":"... or you can go with <b>The Pack</b> book route - and give your non-Uratha packmate dicepools of Physical, Mental and Social rolls. You then simply use those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T13:37:59-08:00","id":1357398,"title":"","content":"I use quick and dirty dicepools for NPCs generally. 2-4 dice for something they suck at, 4-6 dice for something they're kinda good at, and 6-8 dice for something they're really good at.<br /> <br /> For conflicts entirely between NPCs, I'm liable not to roll anything and just narrate what serves the story best. If I don't know what will serve the story best, then I'll likely roll things and offer Players the opportunity to throw in positive or negative dice modifiers based on things their characters do to support one NPC over another (throwing a rock, shouting encouragement or insults, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}